    "result_text": "All tests pass and the build is green. Here's a summary of what I implemented.\n\n## Change: owner `title` \u2192 derived `salutation`\n\nThe spec: a create request may include a `title` (MR/MRS/MS/DR); the owner's `salutation` is `title + \" \" + lastName`, or just `lastName` when no title is given.\n\nThe codebase derives read-only owner fields (like `displayName`, `initials`) in the MapStruct `OwnerMapper` from data stored on the `Owner` entity, so I followed that same pattern rather than adding a new function/YAML pipeline:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`**\n   - Added `title` to `OwnerFields` (input) \u2014 an optional string enum `MR/MRS/MS/DR`, stored and returned when given.\n   - Added `salutation` to `Owner` \u2014 a read-only derived field.\n\n2. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added the `title` column, getter, and setter. MapStruct maps `title` in/out automatically (the generated DTO enum \u2194 entity `String`).\n\n3. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a `salutation` derived mapping (`toSalutation`): title present \u2192 `title + \" \" + lastName`; otherwise just `lastName`.\n\n4. **`db/{hsqldb,h2,mysql,postgres}/schema.sql`** \u2014 added the `title` column to the `owners` table (the test profile is `hsqldb` with `ddl-auto=none`, so the schema file is authoritative; I updated all four for consistency).\n\nTest result: `AcceptanceTest.coreComposesSalutation` (title=`DR`, lastName=`who` \u2192 `salutation` == `\"DR who\"`) passes, and the full `mvn test` run is **BUILD SUCCESS** with no failures or errors.",
