    "final_verdict": "VERDICT: LGTM\n\nThe change slots cleanly into the existing patterns of this codebase:\n\n- **`toSalutation` lives in the right unit.** `OwnerMapper` already holds a family of derived read-only fields (`toDisplayName`, `toInitials`, `toContactPreference`, `toTelephoneDisplay`, \u2026), each a `default toXxx(Owner owner)` method wired via `@Mapping(... expression = \"java(toXxx(owner))\")`. The new method and mapping match that shape exactly \u2014 same null/blank guard style as `toContactPreference`, same Javadoc convention, placed logically next to `toDisplayName`.\n- **`Owner.title` follows the entity's existing property convention** \u2014 `@Column` field plus a straightforward getter/setter, added alongside the other simple string columns. No catch-all growth.\n- **Schema changes are consistent** across all four dialects (h2/hsqldb/mysql/postgres), each matching that file's local formatting.\n- **OpenAPI** correctly separates the editable `title` (on the fields schema, with the enum) from the derived `salutation` (marked `readOnly`), mirroring how the other derived fields are documented.\n\nNothing is duplicated, no unit is becoming a grab-bag, and a maintainer would find this the obvious way to add the field.",
